@@ -1,11 +1,12 @@
 # Redis
 
-Rate-limit counters for api-gateway. One pod in `order-platform`, a 1Gi encrypted gp3 disk, AOF on, no password. Not deployed yet.
+Rate-limit counters for api-gateway. One pod in `order-platform`, a 1Gi encrypted gp3 disk, AOF on, password required.
 
 | File | What |
 |---|---|
 | `statefulset.yaml` | The pod and its disk |
 | `service.yaml` | `redis` (what the gateway uses) and `redis-headless` |
+| `externalsecret.yaml` | `redis-auth`: the password from Secrets Manager (`eks-v2-dev-redis-password`), as a one-line config file and as a plain key for the probes |
 | `../apps/redis.yaml` | The ArgoCD app, sync wave -1 |
 | `../manifests/storageclass-gp3.yaml` | The gp3 StorageClass, cluster default |
 | `../manifests/namespace-order-platform.yaml` | The namespace |
@@ -15,6 +16,7 @@ Keep these true:
 - The Service is called `redis` and lives in `order-platform`. The gateway's `REDIS_URL` depends on it.
 - `--appendonly yes`, `--dir /data` and the disk at `/data` stay together. The root filesystem is read-only.
 - `whenDeleted: Delete` stays, or teardown leaves a billed disk behind.
+- The password lives only in Secrets Manager. Redis reads it from `/etc/redis/redis.conf` (mounted from `redis-auth`), the probes from `REDISCLI_AUTH`, and the gateway from `REDIS_PASSWORD`. Changing it in Secrets Manager restarts Redis and the gateway through Reloader.
 - The image tag stays exact (`redis:7.4.11-alpine`). docker-compose still runs `redis:7-alpine`, not aligned yet.
 
 Why it is built this way and the options we weighed: ADR 0006 in Plane (ALPHA-89).
diff --git a/kubernetes/platform/redis/externalsecret.yaml b/kubernetes/platform/redis/externalsecret.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6bc0a2e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kubernetes/platform/redis/externalsecret.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+apiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1
+kind: ExternalSecret
+metadata:
+  name: redis-auth
+  namespace: order-platform
+spec:
+  refreshInterval: 1h
+  secretStoreRef:
+    name: aws-secrets-manager
+    kind: ClusterSecretStore
+  target:
+    name: redis-auth
+    creationPolicy: Owner
+    template:
+      engineVersion: v2
+      data:
+        # Read by redis-server as a config file, so the password is never on the command line.
+        redis.conf: "requirepass {{ .password }}"
+        # Read by redis-cli in the probes (REDISCLI_AUTH).
+        password: "{{ .password }}"
+  data:
+    - secretKey: password
+      remoteRef:
+        key: eks-v2-dev-redis-password
